+# Build Scala with Hindi keywords for Kojo
+
+## Source and scope
+
+- Origin: https://github.com/scala/scala.git
+- Baseline: `v2.13.18`, commit `98f40d00ddcf59a802862d38a9fe79806cde59fa`.
+- Checkout: pinned upstream baseline with the Hindi patch applied; a detached HEAD is supported.
+- Added aliases: `मान` = `val`, `चर` = `var`, `परिभाषा` = `def`, `यदि` = `if`, `अन्यथा` = `else`.
+- English keywords remain supported. Only these five Hindi words become reserved;
+  longer identifiers and backquoted uses remain valid.
+- Build version: `2.13.18-bin-hi`, to identify this modified compiler.
+
+The implementation follows the Turkish compiler patch attached to
+https://github.com/bulent2k2/scala-2/releases/tag/v2.13.18-tr.
+Hindi names are registered in
+`src/reflect/scala/reflect/internal/StdNames.scala` and mapped to existing tokens
+in `src/compiler/scala/tools/nsc/ast/parser/Scanners.scala`. Aliases come before
+English entries in `allKeywords` so diagnostics retain English token names.
+The parser and compiler command-line banner are unchanged.
+
+## Prerequisites and directory layout
+
+Use a JDK, Bash, Git, curl, Python 3, sha256sum, and an internet connection for the first build.
+This build was tested with the Java on PATH: AdoptOpenJDK 1.8.0_265.
+The build bootstraps with Scala 2.13.17, as specified by upstream
+`versions.properties`; the resulting compiler is 2.13.18 with the Hindi patch.
+
+Prepare the workspace using [the shared recipe](../README.md). It contains
+sibling directories `scala/`, `scalariform/`, `tools/`, `logs/`, and `artifacts/`.
+The commands below use the `workspace` variable set during preparation. In a
+new shell, set it to the printed absolute workspace path.
+
+`../tools/sbt` uses the pinned sbt launcher (`sbt-launch` 1.11.7), the sbt version
+specified by this checkout (1.11.7), Maven Central, and a workspace-specific
+sbt global configuration, so user-global sbt plugins do not affect this build.
+It defaults to `java` on PATH, a 2 GB maximum heap, and four active processors.
+Optionally set `KOJO_HI_JAVA=/absolute/path/to/jdk/bin/java`.
+
+If the sibling launcher needs to be restored:
+
+```bash
+curl -fL https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/org/scala-sbt/sbt-launch/1.11.7/sbt-launch-1.11.7.jar \
+  -o ../tools/sbt-launch.jar
+```
+
+## Build and verify
+
+```bash
+cd "$workspace/scala"
+./build-hi.sh
+```
+
+The script performs:
+
+```bash
+../tools/sbt 'set Global / baseVersionSuffix := "bin-hi"' dist/mkPack
+```
+
+It builds the distribution and runs `./verify-hi.sh` against its jars. The full
+distribution remains under `build/pack/`, including command-line launchers and
+optional REPL support jars. This component build does not publish a partial
+release into `../artifacts/`.
+
+After building Scala, run the sibling Scalariform build to test the complete
+set and stage the release:
+
+```bash
+../scalariform/build-hi.sh
+```
+
+Alternatively, run `./build-hi.sh` from the workspace root to build both
+components in order. The final packaging step copies the four release jars,
+writes a checksum file for just those jars, and creates `LICENSES.zip`. Details
+are in [the release packaging instructions](../README.md#package-and-publish-release-assets).
+For an ordinary sbt installation, the equivalent build command is:
+
+```bash
+sbt 'set Global / baseVersionSuffix := "bin-hi"' dist/mkPack
+```
+
+Run only the packaged-jar smoke tests with:
+
+```bash
+./verify-hi.sh
+```
+
+The checks cover Hindi values, mutable variables, functions, constructor fields,
+English/Hindi mixing, conditional branches, nested and chained conditionals,
+evaluation of only the selected branch, longer Hindi identifiers, backquoted identifiers,
+comments, strings and interpolation. They also reject reassignment to `मान` and
+exercise both `IMain` (using the same constructor as Kojo) and the presentation
+compiler. Sources and the negative-test diagnostic are under `hi-tests/`.
+This does not run Scala's entire upstream compiler test suite.
+
+## Outputs and use
+
+- `build/pack/lib/scala-library.jar`
+- `build/pack/lib/scala-reflect.jar`
+- `build/pack/lib/scala-compiler.jar`
+- Staged copies after the full build: `../artifacts/scala-{library,reflect,compiler}.jar`.
+
+Keep these three jars together rather than mixing them with stock Scala jars.
+Build the sibling Scalariform checkout using its `BUILD-HI.md` to complete the
+four-jar Kojo toolchain. No existing Kojo installation is modified by these scripts.
+
+Example after the full release has been staged:
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p hi-tests/target
+java -cp '../artifacts/*' scala.tools.nsc.Main -usejavacp -encoding UTF-8 \
+  -d hi-tests/target hi-tests/HindiKeywordsSmoke.scala
+java -cp 'hi-tests/target:../artifacts/*' HindiKeywordsSmoke
+```
+
+The shared recipe captures the complete build and verification output in
+`../logs/build.log`.
+
+## Verified result
+
+The initial distribution build and the complete `build-hi.sh` run succeeded
+on Java 1.8.0_265. Batch compilation, IMain, presentation-compiler and
+val-reassignment checks all passed.
